Q: Why does checkbox size change during transition? A: <p>This is the result of subpixel rounding, more specifically the result of the padding on your <code>label</code>.</p>
<p>Adjusting to <code>padding: 0.21em;</code> resolved the issue for me at zooms I could reproduce at without adjusting the layout, though you will need to do more extensive testing to see if this correctly rounds on all browsers your project supports, as well as with your base measurement for ems.</p>
<p>This works because: often, adding a hundredth (or other small fraction) can resolve subpixel issues like this by making the browser round consistently up or down.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code> body:has(#show-expert-settings:not(:checked)) .expert-settings {
  visibility: hidden;
  height: 0;
  padding-block: 0;
}

.expert-settings {
  transition: height 1s, visibility 1s allow-discrete, padding-block 1s;
  @starting-style {
    height: 0;
    padding-block: 0;
  }
  interpolate-size: allow-keywords;
}

fieldset {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  max-width: 200px;
  width: max-content;
}

label {
  overflow: hidden;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  padding: 0.21em;
  width: min-content;
}

body {
  font-family: Tahoma;
}</code></pre>
